{
  "paper": {
    "title": "Earth-sized tests of long-range neutrino interactions",
    "authors": [
      "Dyer F. Cárdenas",
      "Mauricio Bustamante"
    ],
    "arxiv": "to be added",
    "repository": "https://github.com/mbustama/nu-lri-earth"
  },
  "content": "One-sided upper limits on the coupling of the Z' of 14 flavor-dependent U(1)' symmetries (15 entries: L_mu - L_tau for either sign of its charge factor), from 8 years of public IceCube DeepCore data, with a livetime of 2724 days (7.5 years) and with the potential of the Earth computed at every point along the path of each neutrino; and the bounded intervals of couplings excluded for the two symmetries whose potential acts on nu_e alone with k < 0.",
  "how_to_read": {
    "mediator_mass_eV": "The 25 mediator masses m' of the analysis, 1e-15 to 1e-9 eV, four per decade.",
    "interaction_range_km": "The interaction range 1/m' = (hbar c)/m' at each mass, with hbar c = 1.97327e-10 eV km.",
    "upper_limit": "upper_limit[CL][data][i] is the upper limit on the coupling at mediator_mass_eV[i]: CL is '90' or '95' (% confidence level), data is 'observed' (the DeepCore data) or 'expected' (the Asimov data set: the expected events of the fit without a long-range interaction). null: no upper limit at that mass. upper_limit is null for a symmetry with none at any mass.",
    "coupling": "The coupling bounded: g', the gauge coupling of the U(1)'; for L_mu - L_tau, which matter does not carry, the effective coupling G' = [g' (xi - sin(theta_W) chi)]^(1/2) of the mixing between the Z' and the Z, with xi and chi as in the paper.",
    "charge_factor_k": "The charge factor of the paper's Table I: the potential is g'^2 k times a potential per electron, on the flavors of potential_acts_on. The limits on the effective coupling g' sqrt|k| (the paper's Fig. 8) follow by multiplying upper_limit by sqrt(|k|).",
    "excluded_intervals": "For L_e + 2L_mu + 2L_tau and B_y + L_mu + L_tau: excluded_intervals[CL][data] lists, at each mass where there is one, the interval of g' from g_lower to g_upper that is excluded; none at 95% C.L.",
    "statistics": "At each mass, Delta chi^2(g'^2) = chi^2 at g'^2 minus chi^2 at the best-fit g'^2 >= 0, each minimized over the 18 nuisance parameters of the DeepCore analysis and the six oscillation parameters (theta_23 and Delta m^2_31 free; NuFIT 6.1 priors on the other four). The upper limits are where Delta chi^2 = 1.64 (90% C.L.) and 2.71 (95% C.L.), the thresholds for a one-sided limit at the boundary g'^2 = 0 (the paper's Sec. III and Appendix E)."
  },
